  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "python-brotlicffi security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for python-brotlicffi is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Python CFFI bindings to the Brotli library.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA buffer overflow vulnerability in the Brotli decoder (c/dec/decode.c) in Google Brotli versions 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 on all platforms allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to corrupt adjacent decoder state memory, disclose sensitive memory contents, cause a denial of service, or potentially execute arbitrary code using a crafted Brotli-compressed stream.\n\n\n\n\n\nUsers need to update any Brotli libraries or binaries between 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 to the latest available version: 1.0.10 or 1.1.1 or 1.2.1.(CVE-2026-111497)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for python-brotlicffi is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of critical. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Critical",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "python-brotlicffi",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
